 "title": "Moral Luck",
 "dates": "Sunday, September 13 – Friday, September 18, 2009",
 "logline": "Sunday the Saints open at ten in the morning, Monday Hale asks whether luck can make a man guilty, and Thursday is Bid Day — wear something you can cry in.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Lena walked out of Café Bastille in the middle of a song called “Fresno.” You went after her.",
   "if": "e4_followed==\"now\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At the end of the harbor pier she told you about her grandmother: the storm, four days, a medal that came back in a plastic bag."
  },
  {
   "text": "You told her your brother is in prison. She didn’t ask what for. She asked his name.",
   "if": "lena_knows_danny"
  },
  {
   "text": "In Hale’s seminar you said the old general is still the boy who robbed the orchard. “You don’t get out of a thing by forgetting it.”",
   "if": "e4_seminar==\"same\""
  },
  {
   "text": "She walked home three miles in your brother’s jacket. On the steps you counted the freight together, and she said, “Thank you, Jack.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Saturday night at the Anchor: “WHO DAT. One day. Ten a.m., Sully’s. Black and gold or don’t come.”"
  }
 ],
